.\" dentisys-toolkit.8 - manual page for the DentiSYS sysadmin toolkit (IT 123, Option 1B).
.\" Based on the template in Appendix C of the IT 123 Final Project Guide.
.\" AI use: drafted with Claude Code (Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5) from the group's
.\"         2026-11-23 version (written without AI), then reviewed and explained. README 7.
.\" View it with: man ./dentisys-toolkit.8
.TH DENTISYS-TOOLKIT 8 "2026" "Group 07" "DentiSYS Administration"
.\" .nh: do not hyphenate words, so paths and options stay whole.
.nh
.SH NAME
dentisys-toolkit \- service lifecycle scripts for DentiSYS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dentisys-install.sh
[\-\-port PORT] [\-\-mail\-port PORT] [\-\-dean\-email ADDRESS] BUNDLE
.br
.B dentisys-service.sh
start | stop | restart
.br
.B dentisys-status.sh
[\-\-watch SECONDS] [\-\-count N] [\-\-save]
.br
.B dentisys-update.sh
BUNDLE
.br
.B dentisys-pause.sh
pause | resume | status
.br
.B dentisys-maintenance.sh
on [MESSAGE] | off | status
.PP
Every script also accepts
.B \-\-help
and must be run as root (with
.BR sudo ).
.SH DESCRIPTION
The DentiSYS toolkit installs and controls DentiSYS, our capstone web system
(grades, attendance, user accounts), on an Ubuntu Server
24.04 machine. DentiSYS runs as five Docker containers that start in this order:
.B db
(PostgreSQL),
.B mailpit
(test e-mail viewer),
.B biometric
(face recognition),
.B web
(PHP backend) and
.B frontend
(nginx). The six scripts install the application from an offline bundle, start
and stop it in the correct order, report its state, back it up before an update,
freeze and resume its processes, and show a maintenance page. They are used by
the server administrator. All scripts load the shared file
.BR dentisys-lib.sh ,
and only one toolkit script can change the system at a time (a lock file).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B dentisys-install.sh \fR[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIBUNDLE
Installs DentiSYS on a clean server from
.IR BUNDLE ,
a
.I dentisys-VERSION.tar.gz
file. It installs Docker and Docker Compose with
.BR apt-get ,
checks that both ports are free, creates the
.B dentisys
service user and group (no login shell), checks the bundle with
.BR sha256sum ,
copies the application to
.IR /opt/dentisys ,
loads the Docker images, writes new random secrets to
.I /etc/dentisys/dentisys.env
(mode 600), sets ownership and permissions, starts the services (the database
container creates the database and its user on first start), and checks that the
application responds. It ends with SUCCESS or FAILURE.
Options:
.B \-\-port
(application port, default 8080),
.B \-\-mail\-port
(Mailpit port, default 8025),
.B \-\-dean\-email
(the first Dean account; its invitation goes to Mailpit). A run that stopped
halfway can be repeated; a second run after a successful install is refused.
.TP
.B dentisys-service.sh start\fR|\fBstop\fR|\fBrestart
.B start
starts the services one at a time in the order db, mailpit, biometric, web,
frontend, and waits for each to be healthy before the next. It refuses to start
a second copy when DentiSYS is already running.
.B stop
stops them in the reverse order and also ends maintenance mode.
.B restart
runs stop, then start.
.TP
.B dentisys-status.sh \fR[\fB\-\-watch \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-\-count \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-save\fR]
Reports the installed version, the state of each service, the TCP port the
application listens on (from
.BR ss ),
whether the application and its database answer the health check, CPU and
memory per container (from
.BR "docker stats" ),
and the server's load average, memory
.RB ( free )
and disk
.RB ( df ).
.B \-\-watch
repeats the report every
.I SECONDS
seconds,
.B \-\-count
stops after
.I N
reports, and
.B \-\-save
also writes each report to
.IR /var/log/dentisys/status-DATE.txt .
.TP
.B dentisys-update.sh \fIBUNDLE
Updates DentiSYS to the version in
.IR BUNDLE .
It checks the bundle's checksums, then backs up the database
.RB ( pg_dump )
and
.I /opt/dentisys
into one dated archive in
.IR /var/backups/dentisys ,
and verifies it with
.B gzip \-t
and
.BR "tar \-tzf" .
It then loads the new images, copies the new files, runs pending database
migrations, recreates the containers, and checks the application. If the check
fails, it does not undo the update: it prints a framed UPDATE FAILED message with
the three exact commands to restore the backup by hand, and exits with status 7.
It refuses a bundle whose version is already installed.
.TP
.B dentisys-pause.sh pause\fR|\fBresume\fR|\fBstatus
.B pause
sends SIGSTOP
.RB ( "kill \-STOP" )
to every process of the frontend, web and biometric containers; their process
IDs come from
.BR "docker top" .
Nothing answers until
.B resume
sends SIGCONT
.RB ( "kill \-CONT" ).
The database keeps running.
.B status
lists the processes and their state (T means stopped).
.TP
.B dentisys-maintenance.sh on \fR[\fIMESSAGE\fR]|\fBoff\fR|\fBstatus
.B on
stops the front end and starts an nginx container on the same port that answers
every request with HTTP 503 and a "DentiSYS is temporarily unavailable" page
showing
.I MESSAGE
(for example the time the system will be back). Unlike pause, the server keeps
answering.
.B off
removes the page and starts the front end again.
.B status
says whether maintenance mode is on.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install version 1.0 on ports 8090 and 8026:
.PP
.B sudo ./dentisys-install.sh \-\-port 8090 \-\-mail\-port 8026 \-\-dean\-email dean@bicol-u.edu.ph /root/dentisys-1.0.tar.gz
.PP
Stop and start the application:
.PP
.B sudo ./dentisys-service.sh stop
.br
.B sudo ./dentisys-service.sh start
.PP
Three status reports, five seconds apart, each saved to a file:
.PP
.B sudo ./dentisys-status.sh \-\-watch 5 \-\-count 3 \-\-save
.PP
Back up and update to version 1.1:
.PP
.B sudo ./dentisys-update.sh /root/dentisys-1.1.tar.gz
.PP
Freeze the application, then let it continue:
.PP
.B sudo ./dentisys-pause.sh pause
.br
.B sudo ./dentisys-pause.sh resume
.PP
Show the maintenance page, then remove it:
.PP
.B sudo ./dentisys-maintenance.sh on """Back at 3:00 PM today."""
.br
.B sudo ./dentisys-maintenance.sh off
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/dentisys/
Application files: Compose files, database scripts, face-recognition models and
the maintenance page template. Owner root, group dentisys, mode 750.
.TP
.I /opt/dentisys/release.env
The installed version and the names of its Docker images. Mode 640.
.TP
.I /etc/dentisys/dentisys.env
Passwords and keys, generated at install. Owner root, mode 600. No script
contains a password.
.TP
.I /var/backups/dentisys/dentisys-backup-DATE-vVERSION.tar.gz
Backup made by dentisys-update.sh before each update (application files and
database dump), with a
.I .sha256
checksum file beside it. Directory mode 700.
.TP
.I /var/log/dentisys/
Install logs (install-DATE.log), update logs (update-DATE.log) and saved status
reports (status-DATE.txt).
.TP
.I /var/lib/dentisys/maintenance/
The maintenance page and nginx configuration in use while maintenance mode is on.
.TP
.I /run/dentisys/
The lock file (toolkit.lock) and the pause marker (paused). Cleared at reboot.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error: bad input, file not found, a step failed, or DentiSYS is already
installed.
.TP
.B 2
Not run as root.
.TP
.B 3
A required command is missing.
.TP
.B 4
Another toolkit script is running (the lock is taken).
.TP
.B 5
Wrong state: already running, already paused, paused, or maintenance mode is
already on or not on.
.TP
.B 6
dentisys-status.sh only: DentiSYS is not running or not healthy.
.TP
.B 7
dentisys-update.sh only: the update was applied but the check failed. Restore
the backup by hand with the commands the script printed.
